# The Forgejo releases the lab may run (crates/puddle-e2e/src/lab/forgejo.rs): `<version> <release asset> <sha256>`.
# Forgejo ships no Windows build (it dropped Windows support), so the Windows tier runs Gitea, the project Forgejo
# forked from, from Gitea's own release (https://dl.gitea.com/gitea/<version>/<asset>, checksum from <asset>.sha256);
# the fixture's commands and the app.ini it writes are the same for both.
# ci/fetch-forgejo.sh refuses a download that is not listed here or does not match. The first line is
# the version it fetches by default. The value is the SHA-256 Forgejo publishes beside the asset
# (<asset>.sha256 on https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/releases), checked against a download.
17.0.1 forgejo-17.0.1-linux-amd64 51a8cdf4a1252e79f4b3855d7a7891af6c6635105420768c460e2f0690385d6f
28.3.0 gitea-28.3.0-windows-amd64.exe 4003c068ef0a7d8145ef8c85b8aab052bf1bbf9226f2d0058572f013e096ee06
